ICS-OS is an educational operating system based on Dex-OS (http://sourceforge.net/projects/dex-os)

(c) Institute of Computer Science, University of the Philippines Los Banos

## ics-os-ex extensions

This checkout is the **x86-64 long-mode** instructional kernel:

- **x86-64 long mode** (`Kernel64.bin`, Multiboot2) — see `docs/smp-longmode.md`
- **Software context switch** + priority round-robin scheduler
- **LAPIC / SMP** (`make test-smp` defaults to four vCPUs;
	`make test-smp-matrix` validates 1/2/4/8)
- **In-OS GCC kernel rebuild/kexec** (`make test-kbuild`; compiler closure certification pending), **ELF64 user exec** (`make test-exec`), and optional **x86_64 TinyCC** (`make test-selfhost`)
- FAT16 **ramdisk** at `/ramdisk`; ISO9660 CD root; 8.3 `tccsrc.tar` staging for `tccboot`
- Console tests: `kbuild` (GCC), `tcckbuild` (optional), `selfhost`, `exectest`, `tccboot`, `iobench`, `cc`
- Faster FAT/IDE/USB I/O (extents, block cache, mmap-style exec load)
- Staging: `scripts/stage-selfhost.sh`, `scripts/stage-tcc-short.sh`

Top-level documentation: see `../README.md`.
